ORDINANCE NO. __________

ENTITLED: “AN ORDINANCE AMENDING CERTAIN CHAPTERS AND SECTIONS
OF TITLE 17, ZONING, OF THE CHEYENNE CITY CODE BY
REPEALING AND RE-ENACTING SECTION 17.80.080, SIGNS, OF
CHAPTER 17.80, P PUBLIC DISTRICT.”

BE IT ORDAINED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE,
WYOMING:

Section 1.  That certain chapters and sections of Title 17, Zoning, of the Cheyenne City Code
are hereby amended as set out in this ordinance by repealing and re-enacting Section 17.80.080,
Signs, of Chapter 17.80, P Public District. Sections currently existing within Title 17, Zoning,
and Chapter 17.80, P Public District, not set out within this ordinance remain unchanged.

Section 2.  That Title 17, Zoning, Chapter 17.80, P Public District, Section 17.80.080, Signs,
is hereby repealed and re-enacted to read as follows:

17.80.080 - Signs.

A.
Definitions. For the purposes of this Section, the following term shall be defined as
follows:
"Low-profile sign" means a sign built into or placed upon the ground by way of an
ornamental structure that is not part of a building, and where the surface area of
the structure does not exceed 50% of the sign area of the sign mounted upon it.
B.
Signs are allowed in this district as follows:
1. Wall Signs up to 20% of the wall area, but no more than 400 square feet total.
2. One Projecting Sign per street frontage no greater than 32 square feet in area and
projecting no more than 5 feet from the surface of the wall. A Projecting Sign shall
have a clearance of at least 10 feet from the ground, and shall project no higher than
the wall to which it is affixed.
3. One Freestanding or Low-profile Sign per street frontage or building complex as
limited by the table below.
Table 1. Requirements for Freestanding and Low-Profile Signs in the P District

