### Page 2 of 2

```text
b. Message displays shall remain fixed for at least eight seconds.
c. No animation, video, or other non-static display shall be allowed.
d. No blinking, intermittent, flashing or moving lights shall be allowed.
e. Electronic message centers shall not increase the ambient lighting level by more
than 0.3 foot candles when measured via a foot candle meter at any property line.
Electronic message centers shall have a light-sensing device that adjusts the
brightness as ambient light conditions change to conform to the requirements of
this subsection.
f. Electronic message centers shall not be constructed within 150 linear feet of the
property line of a duplex, single family dwelling, or townhouse located in any of
the following  zone districts: LR-1, LR-2, MR-1, MR-2, or MUR.
g. Transitions between messages shall be accomplished in 2 seconds or less by
employing immediate, dissolve, or fade method.

Section 3.  That this ordinance shall be in full force and effect upon its passage and
publication.

